From 4030ee35959a2cb85e2190f904fae3002b2b89ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.local>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 07:16:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Memorial consistency: one layout system for every memorial
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

AUDIT — the site had THREE templates, not two:
  A  John Peters    1 memorial   bespoke page with its own tab bar
  B  Virginia       1 memorial   MemorialTabShell
  C  everyone else 25 memorials  ONE SCROLLING PAGE, NO TABS AT ALL

25 of 27 memorials had no Journey, no Family Glen, no Family Tree and no
tab bar. That is why memorials felt like different products, and it was
never checked.

NEW — src/components/memorialStandard.ts, one contract every memorial
declares against:
  1. Five rooms, fixed order. No custom top-level tabs, ever.
  2. A room with no content is HIDDEN, not shown empty.
  3. Extra content becomes a SECTION with a sub-nav entry, never a sixth
     tab.
  4. The Memorial room is where every visitor lands.
  5. Exactly one family tree per memorial.

APPLIED — MemorialPage (all 25 dataset memorials) restructured from a
single scrolling page into the five rooms. Its thirteen sections are
regrouped, not rewritten: Biography, Tributes, Scripture, Hymn, Poem,
Music, Photographs, Voice, Booklets and Candles into The Memorial;
Livestream and Life Timeline into The Journey; Resting Place into Family
Glen; and the shared FamilyTree into Family Tree. Sub-navigation is
generated from whichever sections a memorial actually has.

FIXED — Virginia's Family Tree tab rendered the shared FamilyTree AND
FamilyTab underneath, listing every parent, sibling, child and
grandchild twice. The duplicate listing is gone; one tree per memorial.

NEW — src/data/datasetFamilyTree.ts: the Chiimba men share a Glen and now
show together. Every other dataset memorial gets FamilyTree's empty
state, which is honest and keeps the product consistent.

Rooms each memorial now gets:
  Virginia      Journey · Memorial · Glen · Tree · Legacy
  John Peters   Journey · Memorial · Glen · Tree · Legacy
  Tendai Moyo   Journey · Memorial · Glen · Tree
  Chari Chiimba Glen                    (awaiting family content)

9 consistency tests so this cannot silently regress. 43 pass in total.
